Misho, 9 Oct ~22:43Z, through the operations session: „ცარიელი ანგარიშები
წაშალე" — the two accounts the 11:23Z seat-maker clash left behind. There
was no route that deletes a user.

The route deletes the User row only when no table holds anything for the
id. Every user-pointing column is read from the catalogue, so a table added
later is checked too, and each column is compared in its own type so its
index is used (a text cast ran past the timeout on live). Anything anywhere
is a 409 naming the table; a test seat or staff account is held by its own
table and can never be removed; an unknown id is 404; each deletion goes to
erasure_log.

§121 records Misho's night ruling „B, შენი შეზღუდვით" (49242).

